		<Section>Person-First Language and Respectful Communication</Section>
		<Content height="194" width="859" x="170" y="108" padding="20" hasBackground="true" bgColor="#ffffff" bgAlpha="0.9" auto_narrator="true">
			<![CDATA[<p style="font-family: SANS-SERIF; font-size: 28px; margin-bottom: 16px; color:#404448"><b>Person-First Language and Respectful Communication</b></p>
			<p style="font-family: SANS-SERIF; font-size: 24px; color:#404448">Person-first language is a communication approach that emphasizes the individual before their disability. This method acknowledges that a disability is only one aspect of a person's identity. By focusing on the person, it promotes dignity and reduces the stigma associated with disabilities.</p>]]>
		</Content>
		<Flash x="" y="" width="" height="" targetId="" text="" textColor="#000000">swf/empty_1.swf</Flash>
		<Narrator/>


		<Video/>
		<Background>images/670fda9334fab.jpg</Background>
		<navigation/>
	</screen>
	<screen>
		<screen_id x="0" y="0">401</screen_id>
		<Template>4</Template>
		
		<Content height="140" width="1024" x="5" y="404" padding="20" hasBackground="true" bgColor="#ffffff" bgAlpha="0.9" auto_narrator="true">
			<![CDATA[
			<p style="font-family: SANS-SERIF; font-size: 24px; color:#404448">Using person-first language is crucial for fostering respect and inclusion in interactions. It helps build stronger, more positive relationships by acknowledging the individuality of each person. This approach encourages seeing the person as a whole, rather than defining them by their disability.</p>]]>
		</Content>
		
		<Narrator/>

		<Image x="905.000" y="53.583" width="80" height="80" swfSizing="stage">swf/Element_time_clock_white.swf</Image>

