		<Section>Role of a Direct Support Professional</Section>
		<Content height="225" width="859" x="86" y="32" padding="20" hasBackground="true" bgColor="#ffffff" bgAlpha="0.9" auto_narrator="true">
			<![CDATA[<p style="font-family: SANS-SERIF; font-size: 28px; margin-bottom: 16px; color:#404448"><b>Role of a Direct Support Professional</b></p>
			<p style="font-family: SANS-SERIF; font-size: 24px; color:#404448">Direct Support Professionals (DSPs) play a crucial role in the lives of individuals with developmental disabilities by fostering respectful and supportive relationships. They maintain professional boundaries to ensure that interactions remain healthy and productive. Consistency, respect, and professionalism are essential in every interaction to build trust and promote independence.</p>]]>
		</Content>
		<Flash x="" y="" width="" height="" targetId="" text="" textColor="#000000">swf/empty_1.swf</Flash>
		<Narrator/>


		<Video/>
		<Background>images/qBPIZJuiqoPr3hoRAHA7bbAB4rt1TmzWWpCYnLhX.jpg</Background>
		<navigation/>
	</screen>
	<screen>
		<screen_id x="0" y="0">501</screen_id>
		<Template>4</Template>
		
		<Content height="608" width="215" x="0" y="32" padding="20" hasBackground="true" bgColor="#ffffff" bgAlpha="0.9" auto_narrator="true">
			<![CDATA[
			<p style="font-family: SANS-SERIF; font-size: 24px; color:#404448">DSPs are responsible for ensuring the health and safety of those they support, including tasks like hygiene, medication assistance, and safe transfers. They conduct regular environmental checks to prevent injury and illness. As the first line of defense, DSPs must be vigilant and proactive in maintaining a safe environment.</p>]]>
		</Content>
		
		<Narrator/>

		<Image x="431.000" y="161.583" width="77" height="77" swfSizing="stage">swf/Element_time_clock_white.swf</Image>

		<Video/>
