			<![CDATA[
			<p style="font-family: SANS-SERIF; font-size: 24px; color:#404448">Listening for understanding goes beyond hearing words; it involves interpreting behaviors and emotions. Recognizing that behavior is a form of communication helps in addressing the underlying needs of individuals. This approach fosters trust and encourages open, honest interactions.</p>]]>
