		<Section>Emergency Response and Crisis Management</Section>
		<Content height="388" width="549" x="5" y="88" padding="20" hasBackground="true" bgColor="#ffffff" bgAlpha="0.9" auto_narrator="true">
			<![CDATA[<p style="font-family: SANS-SERIF; font-size: 28px; margin-bottom: 16px; color:#404448"><b>Emergency Response and Crisis Management</b></p>
			<p style="font-family: SANS-SERIF; font-size: 24px; color:#404448">Emergency response and crisis management require a calm and composed approach, especially in high-pressure situations. Direct Support Professionals must be trained to identify potential triggers and employ de-escalation techniques effectively. This involves maintaining a non-threatening body language and using a calm, reassuring tone to help individuals regain their emotional balance.</p>]]>
		</Content>
