			<![CDATA[
			<p style="font-family: SANS-SERIF; font-size: 24px; color:#404448">Recognizing signs of abuse or neglect is a critical responsibility for DSPs, who are mandated reporters. This involves being vigilant about physical, emotional, or financial abuse indicators and understanding the legal obligations for reporting. Training in this area ensures that DSPs can protect the well-being of the individuals they support.</p>]]>
		</Content>
		
